## Robustness
- 50 m and 1000 m scales: same null/borderline pattern.
- Climate-control variants (no climate; elev+temp): same pattern (VIF temp 22, elev 14, rain 11; urban VIF 4.9-6.5).
- Excluding Urban habitat (n=567): all null.
- WITHOUT habitat term: n_unint level 1.15 [1.02-1.30] p=0.023; n_total 1.10 p=0.093; n_gard null.
- Stacked pathway-contrast model (plot-clustered SE): no significant pathway x urban interaction
  (Gardening:lvl p=0.29; AgriForest:lvl p=0.063 borderline negative).
- Moran's I on residuals (n_total) = -0.009 (no spatial autocorrelation).
- Overdispersion Pearson/df: 0.75-1.72 (NB appropriate). ZIP unstable (documented).

## Habitat-mediated signal
Urban vs non-Urban plot means: n_total 2.323 vs 0.582 (4.0x); n_unint 1.600 vs 0.326 (4.9x);
n_gard 0.692 vs 0.219 (3.2x); n_agfo 0.031 vs 0.037 (no difference).
Composition (occurrences): Gardening share Urban 30.2% vs non-Urban 40.1% (chi2=3.84, p=0.050).

## Species-level characterization (81 species x pathway rows)
- Unintentional: 60% annual herbs; Asteraceae 11, Amaranthaceae 6, Poaceae 6; success 9.6 plots (AOO 6.2); mrt 104 y.
- Gardening: 47.6% shrub/tree + 42.9% perennial; Poaceae/Asparagaceae/Apocynaceae/Fabaceae; success 3.9 plots; mrt 86 y.
- AgriForest: 66.7% shrub/tree; success 2.3 plots; mrt 106 y.
- 4 species with two pathways (duplicated=TRUE).

## Temporal context
Gardening share of introductions: 16.8% (Before 1500) -> 44.6% (1501-1900) -> 49.0% (1901-1984) -> 75.2% (1985-2019).
AgriForest: 51.4% -> 6.1%. Unintentional: 31.8% -> 18.8%.

## Phylogenetics (81 tips, all matched)
Blomberg K (BM-simulation-validated formula) = 0.650; phylogenetic Moran's I = -0.011
-> invasion success weakly phylogenetically conserved; pathway differences not lineage-driven.
